{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>But Noah found favor in the eyes of YHWH.</b> That is to say: those wicked ones were worthy of being blotted out, and this righteous man was worthy of being saved, for he found favor in the eyes of YHWH. And here the punishment and the reward are explicitly clarified: punishment for the wicked by the waters of the flood, and reward for Noah the righteous man through deliverance and through the finding of favor. And this is what Solomon said, peace be upon him (Proverbs 22:1): ״נבחר שם מעושר רב, מכסף ומזהב חן טוב״ — a good name is chosen over great wealth; favor is better than silver and gold."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 6, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:10:40.910314682Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}